            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_b1bf1b7f">
               <extent xml:id="extent_87b75cdb">6 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_5d89fefd">26 x 34.5</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_57ca29de">3 single folios. Written in ink and pencil. Paper: 18 staves. Sketches for the original first movement and the Finale. With numerous cancellations. On one of the pages dated "21 Februar 1877". On a page with a sketch for a Allegro moderato movement, Gade has used the spare staves to write a draft for at letter: "Dear Mrs. R. I am obliged to be present with a rehearsal in the musical-union to morrow (Monday 12) I therefore propose if it will be convenient for your to take the lesson the day after to morrow (Tirsdag 12). Please give your answer to the servant. / I therefore ask you to permit me to give the usual lesson on Tuesday (Tirsdag 12). If it is convenient to you, please give your answer to the servant."</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
